export anchor SlateToolStyle:
    number: 244
    screen: DesignEditor
    name: Slate tool
    idea: Blue-grey professional tool chrome with a compact 11px UI, clear ruled panels and one working blue, built for long sessions in a design tool.
    base: dark
    palette:
        well: #161a20, the page and the canvas behind a 16px dot grid in #2c333e
        chrome: #1a1f27, the top bar, the status bar and number fields
        panel: #222831, the layers panel and the inspector
        line: #353d49, every panel edge and section rule
        ink: #dbe1ea, text
        muted: #9ba6b5, panel labels, layer type icons and field prefixes
        accent: #2f6fde, the active tool and the Share button under white text
        accentInk: #8fb6ff, the Selected tag, the selected row edge, tab underline and focus
        row: #2c3a52, the selected layer row and the active direction segment
        saved: #62d29d, the Saved text and icon
        guide: #ff6ba6, spacing guides with dark label text
        pin: #f2b84b, the comment pin behind dark initials
    type:
        One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
        Arial, with ui-monospace for zoom, sizes and number fields. Base
        11px at 1.4. Panel heads are 11px 600 caps tracked 0.06em, the file
        name 11px 600, values 11px mono, and the style sheet title 22px.
    layout:
        A classic three panel desktop tool. A 40px top bar holds a blue B
        square, the file name over Canvas and Home v3, a recessed group of
        six icon tools with Move filled blue, then the three overlapping
        initials discs, a mono zoom box with a chevron, an icon Present
        button and a blue Share button. Below, a 232px layers panel with
        Layers and Assets tabs and 24px tree rows, the canvas in the middle
        with a dot grid, and a 248px inspector with Design and Prototype
        tabs. The inspector stacks ruled sections for Frame with a two by
        two X Y W H grid, Auto layout with a Vertical and Horizontal
        segment plus gap and padding fields, Corner radius, Fill with a
        white swatch and Export with format, scale and an Export Hero
        button. A 24px status bar runs along the bottom. The Hero frame
        sits white with a blue outline, eight square handles, a blue size
        badge below and the comment bubble in chrome colour. Below 760px
        the side panels and top tools hide, and a bottom bar of six 44px
        tools appears above a wrapping status bar.
    spacing: A 4px unit. 24px rows, 28px panel heads, 8 to 10px panel padding, 40 to 48px around the frame.
    density: Dense. Three panels and a status bar always visible with small type.
    corners: Small. 3 to 4px on fields, buttons and the tool group, square panels, round avatars.
    borders: 1px #353d49 between every panel and inspector section. The selected layer row adds a 2px accentInk inner left edge.
    shadows: None on panels. Only the comment bubble floats with 0 4px 12px black at 40 percent.
    icons:
        16px line icons at 1.5px stroke with round caps, 14px inside panels.
        Layer types use a hash for frames, a T for text, a nested diamond
        for the component instance in soft violet and a picture for the
        image. Saved uses a check circle, editing uses two people and the
        version uses a tag, each with its words.
    focus: A 2px #8fb6ff outline offset 1px. Number fields add a 1px inner ring in the same blue.
    tone: Terse tool labels, such as Design, Auto layout and Export Hero.
